// BSON - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# A BSON document of one string field. BSON is length-prefixed: the first
# four bytes are the total length including themselves and the terminator,
# then the type byte 0x02 for string, the NUL-terminated key, the string's
# own little-endian length, its bytes, a NUL, and a document terminator.
0000  20 00 00 00 02 67 72 65 65 74 69 6E 67 00 0C 00 | ....greeting...|
0010  00 00 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 21 00 00 |..Hello World!..|
